  "id": "budget-ou8p",
  "title": "Renaming rules: a new or changed rule applies only to transactions imported from then on; add 'Apply to past transactions' on the rule",
  "description": "Owner decision 2026-11-25 (Inbox thread 'Transfers refactor'): 'No by default, with an Apply to past transactions button on the rule'. Today (main and after budget-mkrt) adding or editing a rule re-points untouched bank-synced rows at the next sync and makes a statement re-import duplicate them (see review-mkrt.md 'RULE ADDED OR EDITED LATER' and review-mkrt-3.md F8 on budget-mkrt). Server: a rule carries the time it was created or last changed; a sync or re-import never changes the payee of a row imported before that time because of the rule (rows inserted afterwards, and rows whose bank text really changes, take it). New operation to apply one rule to past rows on purpose: a dry run that returns how many rows would change and a sample, then apply in one transaction, budget-scoped, only rows whose stored bank text matches and that the user has not edited, keeping import keys so re-import still dedupes, undoable or at least reported; a rule on a transfer payee creates hints for the matcher, never mirrors. Client: the button on the rule row comes with the Manage Payees task.",
  "status": "closed",
  "priority": 1,
  "issue_type": "task",
